## Part 3: Known Gaps & Honest Limitations

| # | Gap | Severity | Where It Breaks | Fix Sprint |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **G1** | No auth on EAIA endpoints | 🔴 Critical | Anyone with the URL can fire pipelines / send emails | Sprint 1 |
| **G2** | No deliverability layer (SPF/DKIM/warmup) | 🔴 Critical | Emails may land in spam at scale | Sprint 5 |
| **G3** | Reply classifier is keyword-only | 🟡 Medium | Sarcasm, foreign languages, nuanced replies misclassified | Sprint 4 |
| **G4** | Duplicate classifiers (inbound.py vs mcp_server.py) | 🟡 Medium | Different keyword lists → inconsistent classification | Sprint 4 |
| **G5** | No real-time frontend updates | 🟡 Medium | After webhook events, UI requires manual refresh | Sprint 2 |
| **G6** | No PubMed/arXiv direct query | 🟢 Low | Academic publications found inconsistently via Tavily | Sprint 7 |
| **G7** | No YouTube/podcast transcript extraction | 🟢 Low | Video content URLs found but not parsed | Sprint 7+ |
| **G8** | No "drafts inbox" — emails fire immediately | 🟡 Medium | No human review before Day 0 send (unless quarantined) | Sprint 1 |
| **G9** | Cohere-only for email writing (no fallback) | 🟡 Medium | If Cohere is down, write_node fails entirely | Sprint 2 |
| **G10** | 6 MCP tools have no agent usage path | 🟢 Low | Capabilities exist but aren't wired into any workflow | Sprint 3 |
| **G11** | Hardcoded Enrichment Sources | 🔴 Critical | Pipeline only fires Finance sources. 3 orphaned capability systems (BioMed MCP, PI Intelligence Extractor) never compose into the pipeline. A healthcare investor gets zero clinical context. | Sprint 2 |

